# Ignore snapshot CONTENTS (large ad-hoc exports) but keep descending so the two
# tracked source files below can be re-included. `snapshots/` (dir form) would
# stop git descending and defeat the negations.
snapshots/*
# Track the P1AZ policy generator AND its reconcile-base/import artifact: the
# generator reconciles INTO the snapshot (does not rebuild it from scratch), so
# both are source. Other large ad-hoc exports under snapshots/ stay ignored.
!snapshots/gen-authorize-snapshot.js
!snapshots/Super_Banking_Transaction_Authorization_P1AZ.snapshot.json
# Track the snapshot regression tests too — otherwise `snapshots/*` hides them and
# `test:snapshots` runs zero files (exit 0) on a clean CI checkout, i.e. the
# drift/cloud-delta protection silently never runs. scripts/test-snapshots.sh
# fails loudly if the glob ever matches nothing again.
!snapshots/authorizeSnapshotDrift.test.js
!snapshots/authorizeSnapshotCloudDelta.test.js
# Track the MCP amount-bands merger: the gateway makes only the MCP
# decision-endpoint call, so these rules are what give that endpoint an
# amount-aware gate. Ignored, it would never reach the repo and the policy change
# would exist on one laptop only. Its OUTPUT stays ignored — it is a merge of a
# live export and is regenerated per environment, never hand-edited.
!snapshots/merge-mcp-amount-bands.js
